# Each call makes short-lived ordinary objects and gives them their names, as a server does for each request. Between two rounds none of them is alive, and a collection comes just then.
# A collection takes every word on the stack for a reference, so what the calls left there is overwritten first.
# The Structure that an addition leads to outlives an Eden collection while the Structure it comes from is alive, so a round after one files nothing again. A full collection ends them, and they are filed again.
